      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "The relationship of serum cholesterol to the development of major coronary events (CHD) was studied in Italian rural cohorts of adult men aged 40-59 (n = 1672) and of older men aged 65-79 (n = 752) followed up for 5 years. In adult men both univariate and multivariate analysis (the latter with 4 or 5 covariates fed into the Cox model) showed a direct and significant relationship of cholesterol to CHD. In older men the univariate analysis confirmed a direct and significant relationship; for the multivariate analysis none of the considered factors was significantly predictive."},
